  "description": "47 Fountayne Road-Section 73",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The evidence provided is not sufficiently precise and unambiguous to demonstrate that, on the balance of probabilities, planning permission ref: 2021/1912 has commenced within the statutory time frame of three years from 10/09/2019 as required by condition 2. The works undertaken do not constitute material operations as per section 56(4) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.&amp;nbsp;",
    "The proposed changes to the rear dormer roof extension and two additional front roof lights by reason of their size, scale, location and detailed design, comprise an&amp;nbsp;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-038383af-7fff-a2b9-aa46-885dfc2cbe90&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;incongruous, discordant and unsympathetic form of development &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;that is out of keeping with the original building and wider terrace, resulting in harm to the significance of the site and failure to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Northwold and Cazenove Conservation Area. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D1 (London’s form, character and capacity for growth) and D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) D4 (Good design) and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of The London Plan (2021), policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025)."
  ],
